<title>BULGARIA: Sofia, Belgrade restore air links.</title>
<headline>Sofia, Belgrade restore air links.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sofia and Belgrade on Monday restored flights between the two Balkan neighbours, interrupted by a 28-month ban on international flights to and from Yugoslavia that was lifted three years ago.</p>
<p>Balkan Airlines spokesman Viktor Melamed told Reuters a plane of Bulgaria's state-owned airline had flown to Belgrade earlier on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We will fly to Belgrade two times a week and Yugoslavia's airline JAT will fly here once a week,&quot; Melamed said.</p>
</text>
